1. Network Interface and Configuration

These tools help identify interfaces, IP addresses, routes, DNS configuration, and active network connections.

"ip" — Interface and Routing Management

Display network interfaces and IP addresses:

ip addr
ip -br addr

Display routing information:

ip route
ip route get 1.1.1.1

Display neighbor or ARP information:

ip neigh

Why it matters: Before scanning or troubleshooting, identify the interface, local subnet, default gateway, and route used to reach the destination.

"nmcli" — NetworkManager CLI

nmcli device status
nmcli connection show
nmcli device show

Useful for checking connection status and inspecting network configuration.

"ss" — Socket Statistics

Show listening TCP and UDP sockets:

ss -lntup

Show established TCP connections:

ss -tn state established

Display process information where permissions allow:

sudo ss -lntup

Security use: Identify unexpected listening services and investigate which processes are using network ports.

"resolvectl" — DNS Configuration

resolvectl status

Useful for examining DNS servers and resolver configuration on systems using "systemd-resolved".

