8. Web Content Discovery

These tools discover web paths and help inventory an authorized web application.

"Gobuster"

gobuster dir --help

Example against a local lab application:

gobuster dir -u http://127.0.0.1:8000 -w /usr/share/wordlists/dirb/common.txt

"FFUF"

ffuf -h

Example for a local lab:

ffuf -u http://127.0.0.1:8000/FUZZ -w /usr/share/wordlists/dirb/common.txt

"WhatWeb"

whatweb http://127.0.0.1:8000

WhatWeb can help identify technologies exposed by a test web application.

"Nikto"

nikto -Help

Nikto checks for various web-server issues and potentially risky configurations. It can generate numerous requests, so limit it to systems you are allowed to assess.

Important: A discovered path or technology is a lead for investigation, not proof of a vulnerability.

