10. Network Traffic Monitoring and Defense

These tools support network security monitoring and intrusion detection.

"Zeek" — Network Security Monitoring

Zeek analyzes network traffic and generates structured logs for protocols and connection activity.

zeek --version

Review the installed documentation before processing a PCAP or live interface. Log formats depend on the configuration and Zeek version.

"Suricata" — IDS/IPS and Network Analysis

suricata --build-info

Check configuration validity using the configuration file appropriate to your installation:

sudo suricata -T -c /etc/suricata/suricata.yaml

Configuration paths can differ by distribution. Suricata can inspect packet captures or monitor interfaces when configured appropriately.

"Snort" — Intrusion Detection

snort -V
Snort uses rules to detect patterns associated with suspicious or prohibited traffic. Detection quality depends on rule quality, configuration, traffic visibility, and tuning.

What to investigate

- Unexpected outbound connections
- Repeated failed connection attempts
- Unusual DNS queries
- Unexpected services exposed to a network
- Suspicious scanning patterns
- Connections to unapproved destinations
- Abnormal traffic volume or protocol use

Security lesson: Detection tools can produce false positives and miss activity. Validate alerts using packet captures, endpoint logs, asset inventories, and known baselines.

