11. TLS and Certificate Analysis

"OpenSSL"

Inspect a remote TLS certificate:

openssl s_client -connect example.com:443 -servername example.com

Display certificate information from a local certificate file:

openssl x509 -in certificate.pem -noout -subject -issuer -dates

Display a certificate's SHA-256 fingerprint:

openssl x509 -in certificate.pem -noout -fingerprint -sha256

"testssl.sh"

testssl.sh --help

This tool assesses TLS configuration, protocol support, and selected cryptographic weaknesses. Scan only authorized services.

"sslscan"

sslscan --help

"sslscan" can help enumerate supported TLS versions, ciphers, and certificate details.

Security lesson: A valid certificate does not guarantee that an application is secure. Evaluate certificate validity, hostname matching, protocol support, cipher configuration, and application behavior.

