13. Network Performance Testing

"iperf3" — Throughput Measurement

On a test server you control:

iperf3 -s

From an authorized client:

iperf3 -c 192.168.1.10

UDP testing example:

iperf3 -c 192.168.1.10 -u -b 10M -t 10

UDP tests generate traffic at the configured rate and should be restricted to a suitable lab or test network.

"mtr" — Latency and Route Diagnostics

mtr -rw example.com

This can provide a report of route and latency observations. Intermediate-hop loss may reflect router response policies rather than actual end-to-end packet loss.

Useful performance measurements

- Round-trip latency
- Packet loss
- TCP throughput
- UDP loss and jitter
- DNS lookup time
- Connection establishment time

